{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1550774364,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU0MTMwNjc4MTQ=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3174","origin":"github"},"title":"automate check if a PR could be applied to the 0.11.x branch instead?","message":"#### What is the problem?\nNow that \"master\" is to be our next glorious 0.12.x and we want to retain \"master\" as the default branch (aren't we @mih?), I wondered if we could add a check to e.g. travis or appveyor run to verify if branch could  have been applied instead (e.g. if there is no conflicts) to 0.11.x branch.  What I worry though is possible \"false positives\" where a PR just adding a functionality which is not relevant for 0.11.x but wouldn't conflict.  So may be there is just a service we could inform us (instead of travis or appveyor failing) if branch could be applied to 0.11.x and ideally giving a \"git rebase\" command to run to achieve it (since it would have all needed information I believe, unless github branch name differs).","files":null}]}